  "body": "#1186: the project loader refused a tool with bad numbers. The message was `tool parameters are not usable: ToolDto { ... }`, with the full structure. The refusal was correct, but it did not name the tool or the field. `AddTool` and `ChangeTool` printed a similar dump. The library import and the library reader gave a general message.\n\nThe branch has upstream main at a529c455, merged in.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`Tool::why_not_sane() -> Option<String>`** (new file `crates/tools/src/tool_sanity.rs`). It gives the first rule that a tool breaks, in plain words. Examples:\n  - `turning surface speed 0 m/min is outside 0..2000 m/min (it must be over 0)`\n  - `corner radius 100 mm is more than half the 6 mm diameter`\n  - `a drill's tip angle 50 degrees must be over 60`\n  - `a sinker electrode turns no spindle: its spindle speed must be 0, not 1000 rpm`\n  - `TurningData::why_not_sane` gives the same for the turning limits.\n- **One source of truth.** `Tool::is_sane` and `TurningData::is_sane` are now `why_not_sane().is_none()`. Thus the message and the verdict cannot be different. The rules moved out of `tools.rs` in the same order, with the same limits.\n- **The rules that main added are included.** Main added these after the branch started:\n  - the `pitch_min` field;\n  - the waterjet, electrode and thread-mill kinds and their rules;\n  - the catalog and cutting-row refusals.\n  - Each of these rules has its own message now.\n- **Four refusals now read `tool '<name>': <rule>`:**\n  - the project loader (`project/validate.rs`), which is the case in the issue;\n  - `AddTool` and `ChangeTool` (`commands/tool.rs`);\n  - the tool-library import (`commands/tool_import.rs`);\n  - the library reader (`tool_library.rs`).\n  - The MCP tools `add_tool` and `edit_tool` use the same commands. Thus an agent also gets the named rule.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1186-tool-refusal-names.md`.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pinning tests:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/project_tool_refusal.rs` opens a saved file with one bad field through the real loader (`project::open`).\n  - `a_bad_turning_field_is_refused_by_tool_and_field`: surface speed 0, a negative feed per rev, and a max rpm below the rpm of the tool.\n  - `a_bad_milling_field_is_refused_by_tool_and_field`: a corner radius more than half the diameter, and feed 0.\n  - The two tests also make sure that the message has no `ToolDto` dump.\n- `tools::tool_sanity::tests`:\n  - `a_turning_field_is_named`, `a_milling_field_is_named` and `the_newer_kinds_are_named`.\n  - `the_named_law_gives_the_old_verdict_everywhere` keeps the `is_sane` body of main as an oracle. It also keeps the `TurningData::is_sane` body.\n  - The test examines each catalog tool as each of the 17 kinds. It sets each of the 14 numeric fields to 13 edge values: 0, negative, the 60 and 180 degree limits, more than 500, NaN and infinity. It also examines flute counts, orientation codes and turning data.\n  - The new law gives the same verdict in all cases. Thus no tool changes from accepted to refused, or from refused to accepted.\n\nChanged test: `tool_cutter_params::a_reshape_is_refused_by_name_against_the_new_numbers` looked for the old text \"finite and positive\". It now looks for `tool '<name>': diameter -1 mm is outside`.\n\nGates on dbf7799e:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green.\n  - The tools step ran the lib tests and `waterjet`.\n  - The app step ran the lib tests and 44 suites. These include all `tool_*` suites, `project_tool_refusal`, `project_roundtrip`, `thread_mill`, `waterjet_machine`, `plasma_profile`, `mcp` and `commands_undo`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The UI shows these refusals in the status line, as before. No UI test reads their text. A search of `crates/ui` finds none of the old messages.\n- A missing or unknown field is a serde parse error. It occurs before this law runs. The serde message already names the field, and it does not change.\n\nChangelog: A tool refused for unusable numbers (project load, add or edit tool, library import) now names the tool and the rule it breaks, e.g. \"tool 'T1': turning surface speed 0 m/min is outside 0..2000 m/min\", instead of printing the whole definition (#1186)\n\nEffort: low (the label of the issue). Not escalated.\n\nFixes #1186\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
